module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.IsConnected
import StacksCheckRecall

@[expose] public section

universe v u

namespace CategoryTheory

variable (J : Type u) [Category.{v} J]

/- Mathlib's `IsConnected J` is the source-facing owner. Its `Zigzag.setoid` is the equivalence
relation generated by the existence of morphisms, while `isPreconnected_zigzag` and
`zigzag_isConnected` give the two directions of the one-class characterization. Unlike
`IsPreconnected J`, `IsConnected J` also requires `Nonempty J`, exactly excluding the zero-class
empty category. Thus this recall makes no generalization and exposes the standard connected-limit
instances downstream. -/

/- Definition 4.16.1: a category `J` is connected when the equivalence relation generated by
`Nonempty (X ⟶ Y)` has exactly one equivalence class; the canonical mathlib owner is
`IsConnected J`. -/
@[stacks 002S "one equivalence class generated by morphism existence"]
#check (IsConnected J : Prop)

end CategoryTheory
